<title>CANADA: Canada's S. Prairies to be hot, dry to July 30 - EC.</title>
<headline>Canada's S. Prairies to be hot, dry to July 30 - EC.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's southern Prairies on Monday were forecast to see hot, dry weather through Wednesday, an Environment Canada meteorologist said.</p>
<p>&quot;A ridge of high pressure will cover the southern Prairies and bring dry and hot conditions through to the middle of the week,&quot; meteorologist Francois Choquet said in French.</p>
<p>&quot;It's going to be real hot, 30 Celsius (86 F) plus, and it doesn't look like too much precipitation,&quot; Choquet added.</p>
<p>Scattered thundershowers should form over southern Alberta Wednesday and move into southern Saskatchewan Thursday, he said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
